   "szLabel": "Description",
   "szText": "\"The lion coveted the power the barbarian had. So, he prayed to his god for a taste of that strength. When the lion awoke, he wore the man's body, and held the man's severed head in his hands. He devoured the head, ensuring the strength would remain his, and began the hunt anew.\" -Barbarian Folktale",
